<title>AZERBAIJAN: Azeri Jan-Aug oil output down 2.4 pct at 6.8 mln T.</title>
<headline>Azeri Jan-Aug oil output down 2.4 pct at 6.8 mln T.</headline>
<dateline>BAKU 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The former Soviet republic of Azerbaijan produced 6.8 million tonnes of crude oil in the first nine months of this year, down 2.4 percent from year-ago levels, state oil company SOCAR said on Monday.</p>
<p>Natural gas output in the first nine months was 4.75 billion cubic metres (bcm), or 4.6 percent below last year's level.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
